# EPIC-OE-WOLAND-CONSOLIDATED-RESIDUAL-001: Woland residual integration and evidence boundaries

**Epic ID:** `EPIC-OE-WOLAND-CONSOLIDATED-RESIDUAL-001`
**AuthorityEffect:** None
**Status:** `RESEARCH_HOLD`
**Reviewed:** 2026-10-10
**Owner:** Woland maintainers, with native host, OEWAS, OEEIS and OEOS dependency owners.

**Supersedes:** `EPIC-OE-WOLAND-001` through `EPIC-OE-WOLAND-006`. This remains the consolidated residual roadmap; the separate prior-art transition experiment adds source/assumption work and does not replace these integration obligations. The [shared-review reconciliation](../../../receipts/epic_design_review_20261010.md) states the unavailable-attachment boundary.

## Source inspection and repaired obstructions

The previous audit table presented historical test totals as current verified completion. Those totals are removed: source existence and fixture tests are not a production enforcement receipt. [cemetery regression functions](../../../../omega_engine_woland/use_cases/cemetery_regression.py), [OmegaEngineWolandSwarm](../../../../omega_engine_woland/use_cases/base_swarm/woland_swarm.py), [SwarmSpecializationV1](../../../../omega_engine_woland/domain/specialization.py) and [registered profiles](../../../../omega_engine_woland/use_cases/base_swarm/specializations.py) already exist; reuse them instead of inventing V2/V1 replacements or another base swarm.

[execute_7act_woland_bout/WolandSwarmService.execute_bout](../../../../omega_engine_woland/use_cases/bout_service.py) binds candidate checking/carrier measurements through ports. [null adapters](../../../../omega_engine_woland/domain/ports.py) return NOT_MEASURED honestly. [persist_bout_run_folder](../../../../omega_engine_woland/use_cases/persistence.py) delegates custody to native storage. [reconcile_crashed_bouts](../../../../omega_engine_woland/use_cases/bout_recovery.py) closes unterminated bouts as CRASHED_UNKNOWN under a one-writer assumption; it does not resume Act IV seamlessly.

[CochainLens](../../../../omega_engine_woland/domain/residual_algebra/compositional_lens.py) implements forward/backward composition, not complete game semantics with equilibrium/best-response laws. The source-derived idea needs a strategy/utility/axiom map before any open-game or cohomology theorem claim. Local intergate diagnostics implement selected predicates and never authorize native PASS_TO_MASTER by themselves.

## Residual workstreams and dependency decisions

| Workstream | Existing public surface | Owned obstruction and closure evidence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| SAGA1: circle/character selection | [build_parser](../../../../omega_engine_woland/entrypoints/woland_retinue_cli.py) and [WolandBoutController](../../../../omega_engine_woland/controllers/woland_bout_controller.py) | Woland owner specifies scene selection versus live-seat filtering, unknown/empty subset refusal, required terminal/checker seats and profile narrowing. CLI scene success is not native authorization. |
| SAGA2: adversarial intergate integration | [intergate evaluator](../../../../omega_engine_woland/domain/intergates/evaluator.py) and native bout port | Woland/native owners map22 primary,10 intergate and3 empirical gates to applicable acts, evidence sources and PASS/BLOCKED/DIVERTED semantics. Preserve missing metrics, repeated-history evidence and dissent. Quorum/urgency tests exercise production predicates. |
| SAGA3: cemetery/immune loop | `screen_known_regressions`, `ingest_falsified_candidate`, OEEIS adapter | Historical distillation emits ARMED records; that is not human admission. OEEIS/governance settle admitted-catalog trust and healthy controls before new blockers activate. Bind exact payload digests and corrupt-storage refusal before dispatch; reuse CemeteryHeadstoneV1. |
| SAGA4: telemetry/checkpoint recovery | [MultiRoundCritiqueService.execute_critique_loop](../../../../omega_engine_woland/use_cases/multi_round_critique_service.py), native persistence, `reconcile_crashed_bouts` | Woland/OEOS separate CRASHED_UNKNOWN closure from resume; freeze checkpoint schema/writer lease, checkpoint/source/test hashes and sandbox resource/timeouts. Cargo metadata is infrastructure input, not a subprocess in pure AST domain. Current native custody already includes a fifth byte-identical `ddc.jsonl` copy; reconcile the four-file architecture text and version native writer/readers before another file addition. |
| SAGA5: lens/terminal binding | CochainLens, [SymbolGameCandidateChecker.check_candidate](../../../../omega_engine_woland/infrastructure/symbol_game_checker.py), [CandidateCheckV1/parse_checker_receipt](../../../../omega_engine_woland/domain/evidence.py) | Checker owners bind challenge/source/checker trust and receipt bytes before native admission. Native host owns terminal authorization. Lens composition does not establish equilibrium, primitive-difference transport or seven-act correctness. |
| SAGA6: legacy replacement/activation | existing base/profiles and OEWAS008 migration | Inventory callers/archived bytes and verify replacement/narrowing and host activation before removing live routes. Test-local scanner is not production enforcement. Reuse existing profiles; old8/12 counts are not current evidence. |

The disconnected native anti-skill runtime in [OewasAntiSkillAdapter](../../../../omega_engine_woland/infrastructure/estates/oewas_anti_skill.py) stays HOLD until a verified profile-scoped runtime exists. OEWAS007/009 own IC cutover with OEOS writer leases. These are full-scope blockers with owners/closure evidence, not completed deliverables.

## Obstruction review and TDD test plan

The following paths are candidate test files, not authored tests. Each slice is one production behavior: observed RED, smallest owning implementation change to GREEN, then refactor. Existing GREEN controls are reuse. Landau1–5 controls are valid finite input, malformed input, cross-run transplant, concrete counterexample and real production/recovery mutation; mock-only Class0 is insufficient.

### Slice A: authentic checker bytes and terminal evidence

Candidate: `omega_engine_woland/tests/integration/test_native_checker_transplant_contract.py`.

1. Construct one finite C011 request/certificate from the existing challenge fixture; call actual `SymbolGameCandidateChecker.check_candidate`. Independently hash candidate/case/receipt bytes and assert CandidateCheckV1 bindings. Checker acceptance concerns that finite challenge only.
2. Through `WolandSwarmService.execute_bout` with the real native checker path, transplant runA's receipt onto changed runB bytes; require refusal/non-authorized result. Test observers can count calls, but a stub self-reporting ACCEPTED is not the oracle. Missing native host is an explicit failed precondition, never a silent skip/pass.
3. Restore B's checked receipt under a fresh run key. Remove receipt bytes or use null scorer/checker and require NOT_MEASURED/non-authorization. Changed candidate bytes invalidate prior evidence. Refactor only after the focused production-bound case passes.

Inspected mutation target: `CandidateCheckV1.__post_init__` rejects receipt digest mismatch and `binds` matches candidate identity/content. Bypass one guard and require RED; also bind the native consuming verifier before claiming end-to-end coverage. Targets inspected, no mutation executed.

### Slice B: pre-dispatch regression and candidate-only feedback

Candidate: `omega_engine_woland/tests/integration/test_cemetery_admission_boundary_contract.py`.

1. Submit exact buried candidate bytes through `screen_known_regressions` and the composed bout boundary; require REGRESSION_AGAINST_CEMETERY_REFUSED before provider dispatch, preserving the defect witness.
2. Corrupt a headstone/catalog and require typed refusal rather than silently skipping it. A healthy unrelated candidate is the negative-selection control; an unadmitted detector must not obtain blocking authority because distillation says ARMED. Bind the actual admitted-catalog policy before the positive blocking-antibody test.
3. Restore pinned catalog and retry with new candidate/run identity. Emit actual failed result through [OeeisImmuneAdapter.record_candidates](../../../../omega_engine_woland/infrastructure/estates/oeeis_immune.py) and read back CANDIDATE custody with run/task/digest correlation. OEEIS owns the human-admission port; no new admission framework is introduced here.

Inspected mutation target: linked cemetery digest-match/refusal branch. Bypass it in isolation and require zero-dispatch test failure; helper-only cemetery tests do not establish composed pre-dispatch behavior.

### Slice C: interrupted bout and recovery custody

Candidate: `omega_engine_woland/tests/integration/test_bout_reconciliation_contract.py`.

1. Create a real journal start without terminal record, reopen through [the journal store](../../../../omega_engine_woland/infrastructure/bout_journal_store.py) and call `reconcile_crashed_bouts`; require one CRASHED_UNKNOWN closure preserving run/task identity. A second reconciliation adds no duplicate.
2. Inject storage append failure and require BOUT_RECONCILE_INCOMPLETE; recovery never rewrites earlier entries. A valid foreign-run journal is the transplant control and cannot close the current bout.
3. Later checkpoint-resumption testing mutates source/test/checkpoint bytes after interruption and requires refusal before replay. It stays blocked until SAGA4 binds native checkpoint writer/reader, lease and schema; a test-local MCTS graph cannot satisfy that dependency.

Inspected mutation target: `reconcile_crashed_bouts` selects `unterminated_bouts` and appends `crashed_unknown_entry`; bypass append or include terminated bouts and require RED. This remains single-writer reconciliation, not power-loss or multi-worker resume evidence.

### Slice D: circle filtering and residual mathematical contracts

Candidate: `omega_engine_woland/tests/integration/test_retinue_selection_contract.py`. Agree SAGA1 CLI semantics, then add one unknown-character refusal through parser/controller, one valid selected-scene control and one attempted removal of a required checker/terminal seat. Change only the owned filter; narrowing must preserve downstream checks. Recovery is a fresh invocation of the original profile, never reuse of a subset receipt.

For SAGA2 per-act native gates, SAGA4 checkpoints, SAGA5 game semantics and SAGA6 legacy activation, name the public owner/interface before tests. Finite lens law controls belong in existing `omega_engine_woland/tests/test_compositional_open_games.py`, with explicit state/residual carriers and independent forward/backward calculations. A demonstrated lens law does not discharge strategy/equilibrium or general scientific obligations; those remain held under the owners above.

### Theoretical minimum

| Element | Observation |
| --- | --- |
| INVARIANT | Only exact candidate/challenge/checker evidence may reach native authorization; incomplete work retains explicit residuals. |
| BREAK | Transplant a receipt, promote a missing metric or label CRASHED_UNKNOWN as recovered completion. |
| WITNESS | Native boundary refuses/non-authorizes and journal/cemetery retain the failed instance/dissent. |
| MUTATION | Execute the inspected checker/cemetery/recovery mutation against its public-boundary test; record RED/restoration/GREEN. No mutation pass is claimed here. |

### Execution and evidence discipline

Use explicitly invoked [ext-mattpocock-tdd](../../../../.agents/skills/ext-mattpocock-tdd/SKILL.md); its current stub adds no hidden procedural requirements. After authoring, run each candidate file separately from repository root:

```powershell
& 'C:/Users/a343o/source/repos/the_symbol_game/.venv/Scripts/python.exe' -X utf8 -m pytest omega_engine_woland/tests/integration/test_native_checker_transplant_contract.py -q
& 'C:/Users/a343o/source/repos/the_symbol_game/.venv/Scripts/python.exe' -X utf8 -m pytest omega_engine_woland/tests/integration/test_cemetery_admission_boundary_contract.py -q
& 'C:/Users/a343o/source/repos/the_symbol_game/.venv/Scripts/python.exe' -X utf8 -m pytest omega_engine_woland/tests/integration/test_bout_reconciliation_contract.py -q
& 'C:/Users/a343o/source/repos/the_symbol_game/.venv/Scripts/python.exe' -X utf8 -m pytest omega_engine_woland/tests/integration/test_retinue_selection_contract.py -q
```

Four stages: DOC_MGR pins bytes/encoding/links; DEV_MGR with Hella/Azazello binds implementation/budget; QA_MGR/Soviet Inspector run one-to-three files per batch and at most three repair attempts; BUILDER checks theoretical minimum and Woland adjudicates bound evidence with Koroviev dissent preserved. Rust changes use one named crate and `-j 1`. Require actual SoftwareQaReceiptV1 writer/schema before naming any output a production QA receipt.

## Claim discipline

- Supports: consolidated source-inspected residual roadmap with checker, cemetery and recovery experiments.
- Does not support: executed tests/mutations, full design readiness, live admission, automatic native gate enforcement, crash resume, global theorem closure or publication.
- Narrowest claim: existing helpers are reusable and every residual integration obligation has an owner, public-port prerequisite and falsifier.
- Next evidence: author the first executable slice against pinned production bytes; record real RED/minimal GREEN/refactor and mutation/restoration receipts outside the epic folder. Scientific/unbound native obligations remain held.

Cross-epic ownership and retained custody follow the [integration decision](../../decisions/adr_20261010_epic_integration_ownership.md).

## Level Engine consumer dependency

PFP003 owns the explicit [first finite consumer TDD slice](../oepfp/epic_oe_pfp_003_first_slice_tdd_contracts_and_replay_idempotency_plan.md#first-finite-level-engine-consumer-owned-tdd-handoff). SAGA2 composes its findings through the canonical Woland/Moscow service and SAGA5 checks trusted receipt/terminal consumption; neither creates a second research runner. The current LevelEngineRunner.run(challenge_id) takes no candidate bytes, so its thin candidate/fixture/checker/resource-binding adapter remains a prerequisite. Preserve RESEARCH_FIXTURE_REPLAY, canonical custody including the native DDC copy, typed unavailable behavior and zero-provider replay. The PFP003 target is the single acceptance owner; do not duplicate the consumer test suite here.
